[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-ACCOUNTS
TITLE: Account Requirements

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-OWN-ACCOUNT
TITLE: Own Account

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-29
TITLE: Own Account Access
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member open that member's own account on an Account Page that presents Member Information, Account Information, and Password Change sections.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Members manage their own accounts from the Member Frontend. The shared three-section Account Page is the self-service surface.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-90
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-10
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-30
TITLE: Own Account View
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member view that member's own account information in the Member Information and Account Information sections of the Account Page.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member can see the account information held for that member. Section layout and field sets are low-level.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-90
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-10
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-31
TITLE: Own Account Modification
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member modify the Member Information and Account Information that member is permitted to change, including name, contact, addresses, account photo, and username, and SHALL gray membership status and position when that member is not a user moderator.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Self-service account management includes changing permitted fields. Membership status and position stay read-only for ordinary members. Permission switches belong to administrator account management.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-90
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-10
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-32
TITLE: Own Password Change
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member change that member's own password from the Password Change section, with live criteria that report matching confirmation, minimum length, lowercase, uppercase, number, and special character.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR names password change. Own-account management includes replacing the password used for login. Live criteria guide a valid replacement. Password recovery flows that do not require a logged-in Member Frontend session are outside this requirement.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-90
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-33
TITLE: Own Directory Contact Visibility
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member choose which of that member's contact methods are available to fellow members in the members directory.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The members directory shows contact information members make available. Own-account management is where a member controls that availability.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-90
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-10
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-12
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-ADMIN-ACCOUNTS
TITLE: Administrator Account Management

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-34
TITLE: Administrator Account Management Access
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a user moderator open a selected member's Account Page that presents the same Member Information and Account Information sections used for own-account management. Password Change SHALL appear only on the logged-in viewer's own Account Page. An administrator SHALL also receive Password History Reset on any Account Page that administrator opens.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
User moderators manage member accounts from the Member Frontend. An administrator is a user moderator. Sharing Member and Account Information keeps self-service and management visually consistent, while password change stays self-service-only and password-history reset stays an administrator action.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-91
GSSC5-102
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-11
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-35
TITLE: Administrator Account View
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a user moderator view a selected member's account information in the Member Information and Account Information sections.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
User moderators need to inspect member accounts. An administrator is a user moderator. Which fields appear is low-level.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-91
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-11
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-36
TITLE: Administrator Account Modification
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a user moderator modify a selected member's Member Information and Account Information that moderator is permitted to change, including editable membership status and position, and SHALL let an administrator set every site privilege with switches while a non-administrator viewer sees only the selected member's active privileges as a list.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
User moderator account management includes changing permitted fields on another member's account. Privilege switches are administrator-only. An administrator is a user moderator for membership status and position.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-91
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-11
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-37
TITLE: Administrator Account Creation
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let an authorized administrator create a member account.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR names account creation. Administrator account management includes adding a registered member so that member can later log in.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-119
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-ACCOUNT-REFINEMENT
TITLE: Account Page Refinement

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-74
TITLE: Account Section Collapse
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member collapse and expand each Account Page section, with those sections expanded by default.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Long account forms need optional collapse without hiding sections on first open.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-101
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-75
TITLE: Account Form Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL refuse Account Page Member Information and Account Information submission when required fields are empty or format-validated fields are invalid, and SHALL mark failing fields as invalid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Submit-time validation stops incomplete or malformed account updates.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-101
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-76
TITLE: Account Photo File Upload
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL present the account photo as a preview with a file upload control, upload a chosen photo to the Unified Backend account-photos store, and save the returned path on the account.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Account photos are files stored in a dedicated backend directory, not free-text paths.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-101
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-77
TITLE: Password Change Rejection Rules
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL refuse a password change when password criteria are unmet or the new password equals the current password, and SHALL surface Unified Backend rejection when the new password matches a previous password.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Password replacement must meet strength rules and must not reuse current or previous passwords.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-101
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-78
TITLE: Account Mailing Equals Home
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a member mark mailing address equal to home address on the Account Page.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Members often use the same street address for home and mailing. A single control keeps those fields aligned without retyping. No Member Frontend PIR names mailing-equals-home; it refines own-account address management.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-103
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-10
  ROLE: Refines

