[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-40
TITLE: Concurrent Different Page Edits
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let members with the necessary permissions modify different public pages or sections at the same time.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Simultaneous editing of different pages or sections keeps content work from serializing across the membership. Distinct section identities may be held for modification concurrently.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-93
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-22
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-41
TITLE: Exclusive Page or Section Edit
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL limit modification of a given public page or section to one user at a time.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The website does not resolve editing conflicts. One user at a time on a public page or section prevents lost changes when the Page/Section Content Editor holds exclusive modification for that section.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-93
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-22
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-42
TITLE: Edit Contention Feedback
STATEMENT: >>>
When another user already holds modification of a public page or section, the GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL prevent a second user from modifying that same page or section and show that it is unavailable for modification.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires contention feedback. Exclusive edit needs a clear unavailable outcome for the second user so that user does not believe changes were accepted.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-93
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-97
TITLE: Public Section Creation
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a member with the necessary permissions create a new section of a public page from a content template without programming knowledge and without developer intervention.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Authorized members need to add sections to public pages the same way they create announcements from templates, without waiting on developers.
