UID: GSSC-MHLR-SITE-SEARCH
TITLE: Site Search Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-87
TITLE: Site Search Overlay
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL provide a Site Search overlay in the Header that accepts a search query, presents quick results from the Unified Backend Members site search corpus, lets the member open a result destination, and lets the member open the dedicated Members Site Search Page for that query.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a site-search overlay. The Header Site Search control (GSSC-MHLR-86) is the entry point; the overlay supplies quick lookup without leaving the current view, distinct from Directory Search (GSSC-MHLR-DIRECTORY).
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-109
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-86
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-88
TITLE: Members Site Search Page
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL provide a dedicated Members Site Search Page that accepts a search query and optional result-kind filter, presents matching results from the Unified Backend Members site search corpus, and lets the member open a result destination.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a dedicated site-search page. A full search page supports richer filtering than the Header overlay and remains separate from Directory Search.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-109
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-SITE-TREE-EDITOR
TITLE: Site Tree Editor Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-89
TITLE: Site Tree Editor Page
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL provide an administrator Site Tree Editor Page that presents the Public Frontend site tree or the Members Frontend site tree from the Unified Backend, keeps the selected frontend choice and the presented tree aligned from the first presentation of the page, and lets the administrator select a tree node for modification.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a site-tree editor. Administrators maintain navigation destinations for both frontends through the Members Frontend. Presentation of either tree and node selection are the editor entry points; create, modify, and delete behaviors are separate requirements. First-presentation alignment prevents the selector from naming one frontend while another tree is shown.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-116
GSSC5-127
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-90
TITLE: Site Tree Node Creation
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let an administrator create a site tree node under a selected parent in the selected Public or Members site tree without programming knowledge and without developer intervention.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Administrators add destinations to either frontend tree as the site grows. Creation is distinct from modifying or removing an existing node.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-116
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-91
TITLE: Site Tree Node Modification
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let an administrator modify a selected site tree node's label, destination path, optional section tag, sibling order, and parent without programming knowledge and without developer intervention.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Administrators keep destination labels, paths, ordering, and nesting current for Public and Members trees. Reordering siblings and changing parent are modifications of the selected node.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-116
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-92
TITLE: Site Tree Node Deletion
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let an administrator delete a non-root site tree node from the selected Public or Members site tree, including that node's descendants, without programming knowledge and without developer intervention.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Administrators remove obsolete destinations. The tree root stays so each frontend retains a single tree. Descendant removal follows the Unified Backend cascade for the deleted node.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-116
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-99
TITLE: Members Site Tree Permission Visibility
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL present Members Frontend site tree nodes only when the logged-in member has permission to use the destination those nodes represent.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Members site tree destinations include editors and tools that not every member may use. Hiding nodes the member cannot use prevents revealing unavailable destinations such as the newsletter editor.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-127
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-108
TITLE: Site Tree Editor Outline Fold And Pane Scroll
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Site Tree Editor Page SHALL let the administrator expand and collapse nested children under Tree Outline parents, and SHALL keep the Tree Outline region and the Node Editor Panel scrolling independently of each other.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deep trees and long node forms need independent pane scroll so selection and editing stay usable. Foldable parents keep large outlines manageable without leaving the editor.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-138
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-PAGE-DATA-EDITOR
TITLE: Page Data Editor Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-93
TITLE: Page Data Editor Unification
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL provide one Page Data Editor surface that presents public page section editing, announcement editing, and event editing for a logged-in member with the necessary permissions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Separate announcement and event editor destinations duplicated chrome around the shared Generic Editor. One Page Data Editor keeps section, announcement, and event authoring discoverable together while reusing those existing editing capabilities.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-117
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-38
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-43
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-46
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-94
TITLE: Page Data Kind Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member switch the Page Data Editor among section editing, announcement editing, and event editing without leaving that editor surface.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Kind switching is the unification affordance: members move among the absorbed editor entry points without hunting separate destinations.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-117
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-98
TITLE: Page Data Editor Navigation Entry
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL NOT present separate top-level Navigation Menu destinations for announcement editing and for event editing when those editing capabilities are available through the Page Data Editor.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
After Page Data Editor unification, duplicate top-level Announcements and Events destinations confuse members; Pages / Page Data Editor is the entry, with in-editor kind switching for announcements and events.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-126
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-93
  ROLE: Refines

