[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-TEMPLATE-EDITOR
TITLE: Content Template Editor Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-95
TITLE: Content Template Catalog Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL support the Unified Backend content template catalog for administrators who manage templates used when creating page data entries.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a dedicated content template editor. Administrators need a Members surface over the existing Unified Backend template contracts so templates can be maintained without programming knowledge.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-115
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-96
TITLE: Content Template Modification
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let an administrator create, modify, and remove a content template, and set that template's create, modify, and delete permissions by adding and removing readable permission names for every non-administrator permission available to users, without programming knowledge.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Template create, visibility and permission updates, and delete are administrator responsibilities on the Unified Backend; the Member Frontend exposes those operations for day-to-day catalog maintenance, including permission assignment by name rather than opaque numeric values, covering the full known user permission set.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-115
GSSC5-128
GSSC5-141
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

